If you fork this repository for public distribution, DELETE
`fixtures/whale-girl/` first — it is a local-only development aid, not part
of the shipped product.

User pack data (runtime, per-install)
-------------------------------------

Packs authored in-app or imported from `.petpack` files are stored under the
HOST's per-plugin data directory (`<userData>/plugin-data/pet-2d/packs/`) —
runtime data on the user's machine, never part of this repository or its
`dist/`. **Uninstalling the plugin deletes that store** (export packs to
`.petpack` first to keep them). No `.petpack` is ever code: import validates
the container and re-runs the pack contract gate before anything installs —
a user pack is data, and only data.

The whale-girl test-only posture above applies unchanged to every user-facing
path: the compat layer, studio offer, E2E scripts, and fixtures all exist to
PROVE the contract against a real whale-girl-format atlas, and the fixture
never ships.
